    "sentence_translations": [
      "Goose Bumps",
      "",
      "What are “chicken skin bumps”?",
      "The meaning of the characters is “small lumps on the chicken’s skin”.",
      "So how come it is used for a person’s body?",
      "That’s because when we are cold or frightened, we get small lumps on our skin.",
      "And these small lumps are similar to those of a plucked chicken's skin, so they’re called “chicken skin lumps”.",
      "",
      "The word “chicken skin bumps” can be used on a lot of occasions.",
      "When the weather is cold, you can say: “The weather is so cold it’s giving me goose bumps.”",
      "When watching a horror movie, you can say: “This movie scares me so much that I get goose bumps.”",
      "If you hear someone sing, you can say: “Her singing voice gives me goose bumps all over.”",
      "If you see two lovers showing affection, you can say: “You two are too icky, it’s giving me goose bumps.” …",
      "",
      "Have you ever gotten goose bumps?",
      ""
